To visit every element of a two-dimensional list-of-lists, you should use an outer loop for the rows and an inner loop for the columns. For example: 

```python
for row in my_list:
    for elem in row:
        print(elem)
```
Alternatively, you can use index-based loops:
```python
for row_index in range(len(my_list)):
    for column_index in range(len(my_list[0])):
        print(my_list[row_index][column_index])
